<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Debug builds only (gradle source set src/debug — CI's assembleDebug and
  every local `./gradlew assembleDebug`; release builds never see it).

  The E2E dApp fixture is served over plain http from the CI host
  (http://10.0.2.2:8080): Capacitor's local server uses a certificate the
  SECOND WebView does not trust, so https://localhost dies at the cert and
  any other https hop would need a public host. Android 9+ (targetSdk 28+)
  blocks cleartext by default, and run 38031909581 (2026-10-10) proved the
  block: loadStart + loadEnd in the same millisecond, zero bytes reached
  http-server.log, no modal ever appeared, and the journey died at
  "timeout waiting for #confirmYes".

  Production keeps cleartext BLOCKED on purpose: real dApps are https, and
  weakening the shipped transport to suit a test harness would be the wrong
  trade. If a fixture ever has to run on a release build, give it a real
  certificate instead of flipping this flag.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <application android:usesCleartextTraffic="true" />
</manifest>
